# Files a consumer copies into the directory it serves.
#
# The toolchain ships `native/` for the native target but has no equivalent for
# web host assets, so these are copied rather than resolved. The manifest is
# what makes that copy mechanical and checkable instead of a fork — which is
# how a downstream copy of this runtime once diverged silently.
#
# `gpu.js` is NOT here: it belongs to snaidhm, which declares the namespace it
# implements. Copy snaidhm/host/MANIFEST's files too — runtime.js imports
# ./gpu.js and expects it alongside.
runtime.js
sdf.js
ttf.js
raster.wgsl
text.wgsl
image.wgsl
font.ttf
